## Security Limitations

Prompt Shield Phase 1 is a **rule-based heuristic system**. Be aware of the following limitations before deploying in production:

| Limitation | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| **Obfuscation bypass** | Attackers can evade substring matching with typos, synonyms, Unicode homoglyphs, or Base64 encoding (e.g. `Ign0re previous instruct!ons`). |
| **False positives** | Legitimate prompts mentioning security topics may trigger low-level warnings. |
| **Indirect injection** | Phase 1 does not scan documents, URLs, or retrieved context for embedded instructions — a key threat vector for RAG systems. |
| **No semantic understanding** | The detector operates on lexical patterns, not meaning. Paraphrased attacks are not caught. |
| **No rate limiting** | Repeated WARNED requests are not accumulated into a block by default. |
| **No output validation** | The system only inspects *input*; LLM responses are not scanned. |
| **English-only patterns** | Attack patterns are English; multilingual attacks will bypass detection. |

---

## Future Roadmap

| Phase | Feature | Description |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| **2** | Indirect Injection Detection | Scan retrieved documents, tool outputs, and URLs for embedded instructions before they are injected into context. |
| **3** | Document Scanner | Plug-in interface for scanning PDFs, HTML, and plain text files before RAG ingestion. |
| **4** | Output Validation | Post-LLM response scanner to detect prompt-leakage, PII exfiltration, and instruction-following anomalies. |
| **5** | ML-Based Detection | Fine-tuned classifier (e.g., DistilBERT) trained on injection datasets to catch semantic and obfuscated attacks. |
| **6** | Rate Limiting & Sessions | Per-session suspicious-score accumulation; escalating enforcement for repeat offenders. |
| **7** | Multilingual Support | Extend pattern library and ML model to cover attacks in non-English languages. |
| **8** | API Server | FastAPI gateway wrapper exposing `/shield/evaluate` for polyglot service integration. |
| **9** | Audit Dashboard | Web UI for reviewing flagged prompts, score distributions, and false-positive feedback. |

